NNAAMMEE
     diff3 - summarize differences among three files

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddiiffff33 [-ee|-xx|-33] _g_e_n_e_r_a_t_o_r

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ddiiffff33 collates two sets of line-oriented differences -- one
     between _f_i_l_e_1 and _f_i_l_e_3, the other between _f_i_l_e_2 and _f_i_l_e_3 -
     - into one three-way comparison, and either prints a summary
     of where the three files disagree, or, with -ee, -xx, or -33,
     an editor script.

     The two input difference files must already exist, one
     giving the changes from _f_i_l_e_1 to _f_i_l_e_3 and the other the
     changes from _f_i_l_e_2 to _f_i_l_e_3, in the same range-and-letter
     notation that ddiiffff -ee produces.  As shipped in this source
     tree, ddiiffff33 is only the back end that reads those two dif-
     ference files and collates them; it takes exactly one argu-
     ment, _g_e_n_e_r_a_t_o_r, and reads _g_e_n_e_r_a_t_o_raa and _g_e_n_e_r_a_t_o_rbb as the
     file1-versus-file3 and file2-versus-file3 difference files,
     respectively.  Producing those two files (normally with two
     runs of ddiiffff -ee into temporary files named _g_e_n_e_r_a_t_o_raa and
     _g_e_n_e_r_a_t_o_rbb) is the job of a front-end script; no such front
     end is present in this tree (see NOTES).

     Without -ee, -xx, or -33, ddiiffff33 prints a summary in which each
     region of disagreement is headed by one of:

     ====  All three files differ in this region.

     ====_1 Only _f_i_l_e_1 differs (its text is not reflected in the
           region of _f_i_l_e_3).

     ====_2 Only _f_i_l_e_2 differs.

     ====_3 Only _f_i_l_e_3 differs.

     Each header is followed by a line for each of the (up to
     three) files that differ in that region, giving the file
     number, and, in eedd notation, the range of lines and whether
     they were appended (aa) or changed (cc), followed by the af-
     fected text itself.

     -ee   Instead of the summary, print an eedd script that, ap-
          plied to _f_i_l_e_1, carries forward every change that was
          made getting from _f_i_l_e_2 to _f_i_l_e_3 (that is, every region
          marked ==== or ====33).

     -xx   Like -ee, but the script carries forward only the
          regions marked ==== (where all three files differ).

     -33   Like -ee, but the script carries forward only the
          regions marked ====33 (where only _f_i_l_e_3 differs).



